WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:06.120
Casting can make or break a show, and that's
particularly true when it's based on a popular

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.440
book series.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:12.119
When it comes to the beloved Game of Thrones
on HBO, many of the characters don't quite

00:00:12.119 --> 00:00:17.150
match what's written in George R.R. Martin's
books — in fact, in a few circumstances,

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.490
they don't match at all.

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:21.930
Here's how the cast of Game of Thrones should
really look…

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:23.780
Yara Greyjoy

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:28.900
The producers of Game of Thrones changed Asha
Greyjoy's name to Yara on the show — maybe

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.330
to avoid confusion with Osha, the Wildling.

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:33.800
But her name isn't all that's been changed.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:38.949
The novel says she's got "black hair cut short,
and that "her nose was too big and too sharp

00:00:38.949 --> 00:00:41.819
for her thin face, but her smile made up for
it."

00:00:41.819 --> 00:00:45.030
Yara doesn't do much smiling on the show,
of course.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:48.660
But then, with a brother like Theon, you wouldn't
smile either.

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:49.899
Speaking of...

00:00:49.899 --> 00:00:51.589
Theon Greyjoy

00:00:51.589 --> 00:00:56.499
After he was tortured as the prisoner of Ramsay
Bolton, Theon Greyjoy emerged from his ordeal

00:00:56.499 --> 00:00:59.820
mostly unscathed — well, except for his
dangly bits.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:04.560
"Next time you think about naked girls, will
you feel an itch?"

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:10.290
But in the books, Theon was apparently treated
much more harshly, with him getting a gaunt,

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:12.150
skeletal appearance as a result.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:16.360
The trauma of his captivity also turned his
hair white, making him look practically like

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:17.660
an old man.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:24.290
Of course, Theon was probably not so concerned
about his hair by the time he escaped Ramsay.

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:25.740
Ramsay Bolton

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:31.090
On the show, Ramsay is a really ugly person
— but mostly because of his heinous acts.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:36.290
Like the aforementioned torture and weiner-cutting
of Theon Greyjoy, or when he kills his own

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:36.790
daddy:

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:40.160
But in the books?

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:43.490
Martin wrote him as a real uggo.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:47.670
He wrote: "He remained an ugly man, big-boned
and slope-shouldered, with a fleshiness to

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:50.970
him that suggested that in later life he would
run to fat.

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:56.240
His skin was pink and blotchy, his nose broad,
his mouth small, his hair long and dark and

00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:57.240
dry.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.200
His lips were wide and meaty, but the thing
men noticed first about him were his eyes.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.979
[...] small, close-set, queerly pale.

00:02:03.979 --> 00:02:07.040
[...] his eyes were all but colorless, like
two chips of dirty ice."

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:10.710
Ol' Dirty Ice Eyes, that's what we'll call
him!

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:15.780
And does anyone else think that shaggy haircut
kinda makes him look like Glenn Danzig?

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:16.780
Brienne of Tarth

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:21.290
Part of Brienne's tragedy is how much she
wants to fall in love and be loved, but she

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:24.630
knows she's painfully awkward and ugly by
Westerosi standards.

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:29.360
Of course, because this is television, the
showrunners cast the beautiful and statuesque

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.630
Gwendoline Christie for the part, so she'll
never actually be the homely buttkicker described

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:34.630
in the books.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:38.180
Meanwhile, throughout the course of the novels,
Brienne has run-ins with enemies that leave

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:42.210
her even more damaged, like when she got her
teeth knocked out.

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:46.930
Martin wrote that Brienne's hair was "a squirrel's
nest of dirty straw" and that her "eyes were

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:47.959
large and very blue."

00:02:47.959 --> 00:02:52.680
Meanwhile, her "features were broad and coarse,
her teeth prominent and crooked, her mouth

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.790
too wide, her lips so plump they seemed swollen.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:03:00.270
A thousand freckles speckled her cheeks and
brow, and her nose had been broken more than

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:01.340
once."

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:02.960
Sandor 'The Hound' Clegane

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:08.540
HBO's makeup artists did a great job creating
the mass of scars and twisted flesh that cover

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.090
one side of Sandor Clegane's face.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:14.470
It's pretty much perfect...except for one
little thing.

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:16.890
They got the wrong side of his face.

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:19.670
The book says that "the left side of his face
was a ruin.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:22.580
His ear had been burned away; there was nothing
but a hole.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:26.870
[...] Down by his jaw, you could see a hint
of bone where the flesh had been seared away."

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:31.280
Aside from the ear and the bony jaw situation,
the Hound looks pretty incredible.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:34.250
But it makes you wonder what made them flip
sides like that.

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:37.940
Maybe actor Rory McCann just doesn't like
that side of his face?

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:39.020
"Yarp"

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:40.380
Daario Naharis

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:44.710
It's not too hard to figure out why the show's
producers mixed things up for their take on

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:46.150
Daario Naharis.

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:50.400
That's because Daario should've looked less
like a badass warrior, and more like a reject

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:51.700
from The Hunger Games.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:56.030
The novels described Daario as "flamboyant,
with a beard that "was cut into three prongs

00:03:56.030 --> 00:04:00.770
and dyed blue, the same color as his eyes
and the curly hair that fell to his collar.

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:03.090
His pointed mustachios were painted gold."

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:06.599
No wonder Daenerys fell for the ol' gold-mustachioed
charmer.

00:04:06.599 --> 00:04:10.930
He probably picked up his style tips from
the legendary Mystery: The Pickup Artist.

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:15.030
"Meeting Mystery was almost like love at first
site.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:19.290
With his cowboy hat and his medallion necklace.

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:24.090
I was like 'This guy's smokin balls tonight.'"

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:25.090
Tyrion Lannister

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:30.500
Peter Dinklage is just about perfect as Tyrion
Lannister, better known as the Imp.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:34.910
But there's just one problem...and at this
point, you can probably guess what it is.

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:37.770
That's right: he's just not ugly enough.

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:39.000
Noticing a trend here?

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.970
The books describe him as having "squashed-in"
face.

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:46.510
Then, after the events of the Battle of the
Blackwater, he lost about half of his nose.

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:49.780
And finally, he has different-colored eyes.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:51.310
So...yeah.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:52.770
Jorah Mormont

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:57.250
Don't look so surprised...but Ser Jorah in
the books is not quite as handsome as the

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:58.910
showrunners would have us believe.

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:03.650
Our favorite friend-zoned knight is more attractive
and also more lightly built on the Game of

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:06.410
Thrones television series than his book-version
counterpart.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:11.160
Once again, Martin plainly states that this
character isn't going to win any beauty contests:

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.880
"Ser Jorah was not a handsome man.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:18.150
He had a neck and shoulders like a bull, and
coarse black hair covered his arms and chest

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:20.880
so thickly that there was none left for his
head."

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:21.880
Yeesh.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:25.550
Kinda looks like a medieval version of, like,
Clint Howard.

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:26.600
Or Bob Balaban.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:28.770
Or even Wallace Shawn!

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:30.210
He'd make a good Jorah, right?

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:31.660
"Inconceivable!"

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:34.400
Yeah...you're probably right.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:35.400
Never mind.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.400
Thanks for watching!

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:39.240
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:41.660
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love too.

